There seems to be some confusion regarding the ownership of this car.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:22.230
That car?

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:30.000
Janet, tell them whose car it is. Officer, if my wife verified...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.880
there ought to be proof enough for you.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:32.880
Not for me.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:34.700
I'll take it to the Supreme Court.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:36.810
It's amazing. I wouldn't have believed it.

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:37.780
Believed what?

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:41.020
It looks like our car. It's the same make and everything.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:41.940
But it's not.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.020
Not what?

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.020
It's not our car, dear.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:45.020
Janet!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:48.940
Well, there's a little wriggly line in the upholstery of our car.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.940
I told you it was my car.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:53.990
Well, you ought to be glad it isn't ours, Harry.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:56.140
That windshield in the dashboard,

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:58.150
well, it was such a fortune thing.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.150
Officer?

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:01.520
I'll prefer the charges.

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.810
I think we'd better talk to the lieutenant.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.000
Harry, where are you going?

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.550
You have an appointment with Judge Peters.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.390
Tell Judge Peters that I'll see him tomorrow when he sentences me.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:24.380
It was three miles.

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:29.240
You know, Dexter, we can't possibly tell Daddy we ran out of gasoline.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.800
That excuse is just as obvious as the flat tire.

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.720
Well, there's only one thing he's gonna believe then.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.080
We'll have to wreck the car.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.060
Dexter.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.760
You know, if your father doesn't take care of his tires

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.180
or put gasoline in the tank,

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.330
well, he shouldn't impose it on us.

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:46.030
Dexter, the gasoline.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:46.880
What about it?

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:51.640
You forgot to take the cap off the gasoline tank.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.700
It's only three miles.

00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:00.000
Yeah, but there's only one thing I don't understand.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.740
How come it's uphill both ways?

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.600
Poor Dexter must have been born under an unlucky star.

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:20.580
If he inherited a million dollars, the next day Congress would pass a law against money.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.890
we got the car he's not here he left over an hour ago dexter this is catastrophic that means awful

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:52.740
it's catastrophic well i think you'll find him at the club with the judge we'll deliver the car to

00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:53.810
him there come on

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:19.380
explain this to daddy well we'll just tell him the truth that somebody did

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:24.840
trying to steal the car he'll never believe it even sounds like a lot

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:33.910
Well, don't you give it another thought, Harry.

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:36.510
It must have been a terrible inconvenience to you.

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.250
Oh, well, everybody makes mistakes now and then.

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:41.750
Well, you've been a real sport about this, I sure appreciate it.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:44.390
Well, it's kind of an unusual way to make a friend,

00:23:44.390 --> 00:23:48.670
but despite everything that happened, I'm certainly glad I met you.

00:23:48.670 --> 00:23:50.530
Now, don't forget, I want to pay all the damages.

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.040
Well, there's only one thing to do.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.890
Run the car over a cliff.

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:57.240
Sympathy. I'll be in it.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:06.310
Just see if the car gets the Patterson Brothers and tell them to send me the bill.

00:24:06.310 --> 00:24:08.680
Oh, well, that's it.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:14.510
Stealing my car!

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:21.900
Would you mind telling me what's so funny?

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:24.800
Well, Corliss is our daughter and Dexter's her boyfriend.

00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:28.680
Why, you beast, you.

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:30.000
Getting your kids to steal your car.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.000
Oh, no, you don't understand.

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.050
Help! Police! Help!

00:24:34.050 --> 00:24:54.350
Do something, will ya? I can't get out!

00:24:54.350 --> 00:24:56.780
I called a locksmith here.

00:24:56.780 --> 00:24:58.860
He should be here any minute.

00:25:02.940 --> 00:25:05.470
Here he is, Harry. Call us, just let him in.

00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:07.210
Oh, thank goodness.

00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:09.630
Howdy, Mrs. Archer.

00:25:10.490 --> 00:25:11.190
Having a little trouble?

00:25:12.180 --> 00:25:12.900
Well, don't worry.

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:15.780
If I do say it for myself, I'm the best locksmith in town.

00:25:16.120 --> 00:25:18.720
No, no, no, not a guest, not him.

00:25:19.570 --> 00:25:21.460
Don't worry about a thing, Mr. Archer.

00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:23.480
Have you out there in the jiffy?

00:25:23.640 --> 00:25:24.800
No, stop it, Harry.
